    {
      "id": "DfABcZgmvZ23gS_hzDQcA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 34,
      "y": 1085,
      "width": 1692,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "az",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 253960829,
      "version": 689,
      "versionNonce": 511189789,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794330717659,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Compelxity of Merge Sort\n=======================\n\n1. To cal complexity of merge sort we have to cal complexities of spilt and merge separately .\n\n2. The func split () will have a complexity of log n  , because it breaks array into 2 parts on every recursive call .\n\n3. The complexity fun merge () will be O (n) because it compares 2 parts of the same array while sorting . So at most the number of comparisons can never be more than n .\n\n4. Since we are calling merge () from split () on every recursive call , so we will multilpy their complexities and this turns out to be :\n\nC ( n ) = O ( n log n )",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Compelxity of Merge Sort\n=======================\n\n1. To cal complexity of merge sort we have to cal complexities of spilt and merge separately .\n\n2. The func split () will have a complexity of log n  , because it breaks array into 2 parts on every recursive call .\n\n3. The complexity fun merge () will be O (n) because it compares 2 parts of the same array while sorting . So at most the number of comparisons can never be more than n .\n\n4. Since we are calling merge () from split () on every recursive call , so we will multilpy their complexities and this turns out to be :\n\nC ( n ) = O ( n log n )",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
